WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480
On its own, hydrogen peroxide
breaks down only slowly.

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.500
Add a pinch of manganese dioxide
powder, and oxygen bubbles pour out.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.680
When the fizzing stops,
the powder is still there.

4
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.440
Add fresh peroxide, and
it works all over again.

5
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.080
So did the powder take part at all?

6
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:24.600
How can a substance join in a reaction,
change, and still come out unchanged?

7
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.900
In this mission, you'll compare energy
profiles with and without a catalyst,

8
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.860
and see the different route it opens.

9
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:37.480
Then you'll see how a solid catalyst's
surface speeds up reactions between gases.

10
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:43.230
Your mission: explain how a catalyst can join
in a reaction and still be there at the end.